{"created": "2020-06-24T21:30:49.964389+00:00", "modified": "2024-07-19T18:58:41.015598+00:00", "id": 3906947, "conceptrecid": "3906946", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.3906947", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.3906946", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3906947", "metadata": {"title": "Measurements from the debris-covered Imja-Lhotse Shar Glacier (2013-2014)", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.3906947", "publication_date": "2014-07-23", "description": "<p>These data are from the debris-covered portion of Imja-Lhotse Shar Glacier (27.901N, 86.938E, ~5050 m a.s.l.)&nbsp;located in the Nepal Himalaya that were&nbsp;collected during three field expeditions&nbsp;between September 2013 and November&nbsp;2014.&nbsp; The data includes debris thickness measurements derived primarily by manual excavation,&nbsp;debris temperature measurements from thermistors located at the surface or within the debris, ablation stakes, and high-resolution digital elevation models used to estimate the surface roughness. Below is a brief description of the various datasets:</p>\n\n<p>- 15.03743_rounce2014-hd.csv: debris thickness measurements (m) from Rounce and McKinney (2014) and Rounce et al. (2015).</p>\n\n<p>- 15.03743_rounce2014-ts.csv: debris temperature measurements (K) where the depth is reported in cm from Rounce and McKinney (2014).</p>\n\n<p>- 15.03743_rounce2015-melt.csv: ablation stake measurements from the period May 18 - Nov 9 2014&nbsp;detailed in&nbsp;Rounce et al. (2015).</p>\n\n<p>- 15.03743_rounce2015-ts.csv: debris temperature measurements (K) where the depth is reported in cm from Rounce et al.&nbsp;(2015).</p>\n\n<p>- Site_XX_DEM_1cm.tif: digital elevation model used to estimate surface roughness from Rounce et al. (2015).</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>----- Citing datasets -----</p>\n\n<p>If using the debris thickness measurements (15.03743_rounce2014-hd.csv) or temperature data from September 2013 (15.03743_rounce2014-ts.csv), please cite:</p>\n\n<p>Rounce, D.R. and McKinney, D.C. (2014). Debris thickness of glaciers in the Everest area (Nepal Himalaya) derived from satellite imagery using a nonlinear energy balance model,&nbsp;<em>Cryosphere</em>, 8:1317-1329, doi:10.5194/tc-8-1317-2014.</p>\n\n<p>For all other data please cite:</p>\n\n<p>Rounce, D.R., Quincey, D.J., and McKinney, D.C. (2015). Debris-covered glacier energy balance model for Imja-Lhotse Shar Glacier in the Everest region of Nepal,&nbsp;<em>Cryosphere</em>, 9:2295-2310, doi:10.5194/tc-9-2295-2015.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Rounce, David", "affiliation": "Carnegie Mellon University", "orcid": "0000-0002-4481-4191"}], "contributors": [{"name": "McKinney, Daene", "affiliation": "University of Texas at Austin", "type": "ProjectLeader", "orcid": "0000-0002-8345-0028"}], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5194/tc-8-1317-2014", "relation": "isDerivedFrom", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5194/tc-9-2295-2015", "relation": "isDerivedFrom", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "doi"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "communities": [{"id": "iacswgondcgs"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "3906946"}}]}}, "title": "Measurements from the debris-covered Imja-Lhotse Shar Glacier (2013-2014)", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3906947", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/3906947", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/3906947?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3906947", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3906947", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.3906947", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3906947/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/3906946", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/3906946", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3906946", "parent_doi_html"